From 9b5749ac314d95e98067b113adc88cba60aa1f1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Kleber <26285351+kleberbaum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 08:24:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] feat(plugin): answer the PermissionAPI and the commands
 of LuckPerms

On the live server Arclight asks LuckPerms every Boolean node of the
PermissionAPI of Forge for an online player, so who may speak in voice
chat or use spark follows the groups of LuckPerms, while golem run lets
every such node fall to the default resolver of its mod, and the port
of the commands of LuckPerms has no place in the runtime, so no
operator can change the permissions of a running server.

The plugin golem-permissions of the runtime answers every Boolean node
of an online player with Permissions::has_permission, as LuckPerms did,
until the owner rules on issue #105, and leaves a player who is not
online to the default resolver, as Arclight left getOfflinePermission
to it. The native carries no such flag, so the plugin tells an online
player by the game on the server thread and by the operator levels it
keeps from the joins on every other thread, where it asks the game
nothing.

The plugin owns /luckperms and its aliases. A command runs on the set
of the store, writes the entries it changed to the store in their
order and installs the result in the resolver, so the next check sees
it at once. A change the store refuses is logged, answered with the
line of LuckPerms for a failed save, and the set of the store is loaded
again. Every tick hands the resolver a look at the generation of the
store, so a change of another writer reaches the checks.

Link: https://github.com/skytekx/golem/issues/105
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016dYAZEa3eZnoeGd1c8FkBT
Signed-off-by: Florian Kleber <opensource@skytekx.com>
